# Audio, features, and model weights are large and often license-encumbered.
# Nothing under these is committed - see MODELS_AND_DATASETS.md for why.
# The folder patterns are anchored to the repo root. Unanchored, `audio/` also matched the
# src/workbench/audio/ package, which silently kept its source out of git (FIX-1).
/audio/
/models/
*.wav
*.flac
*.mp3
*.aiff
*.ogg
*.onnx
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.zarr/

# Working material
experiments/**/out/
scratch/

# No ignore rules for agent-tooling artifacts. The AI Token Optimizer wrote CLAUDE.md, .codex/,
# .cavemanrc, .aicache/ and .codegraph/; it was removed fleet-wide 2026-11-17 and the rules went
# with it. They were kept briefly as a trap for a reappearance, and that was backwards: .cavemanrc
# sat ignored in four Labs repos for six weeks with `git status` silent the whole time, and it was
# found by listing files rather than by git. An ignored canary is a canary nobody checks. Unignored,
# a regenerated file shows up as untracked and somebody decides; an accidental commit is a visible
# mistake rather than a silent one. LabsHQ ruling 2026-11-17, RT's call.
#
# .vscode/settings.json is the deliberate exception, and for the opposite reason: editor tooling
# still writes it routinely, so its presence is never a signal, and this repo is public - it has
# already carried MCP servers with absolute user paths. Shared editor settings belong in the
# multi-root .code-workspace, which is authored and reviewable.
.vscode/settings.json
